{"name":"Tartan Red","hex":"#b1282a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tartan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Woven woollen fabric with a distinctive pattern of coloured stripes intersecting at right angles originally associated with Scottish Highlanders, now with different clans (though this only dates from the late 18th century) and some Scottish families and institutions having their own patterns;  a particular type of such fabric.","A pattern used on such fabric."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of tartan (noun etymology 1, noun sense 1), or having a distinctive pattern of coloured stripes intersecting at right angles like a that of a tartan.","Of or relating to Scotland, its culture, or people; Scottish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tartan"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tartan","blocks":[{"text":"Tartan, also known, especially in American English, as plaid, is a patterned cloth consisting of crossing horizontal and vertical bands in multiple colours, forming repeating symmetrical patterns known as setts. Tartan patterns vary in complexity, from simple two-colour designs to intricate motifs with over twenty hues. Originating in woven wool, tartan is most strongly associated with Scotland, where it has been used for centuries in traditional clothing such as the kilt. Specific tartans are linked to Scottish clans, families, or regions, with patterns and colours derived historically from local natural dyes. Tartans also serve institutional roles, including military uniforms and organisational branding."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Three_tartans.jpg/330px-Three_tartans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tartan"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Tartans.png/500px-Tartans.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Tartans.png/500px-Tartans.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tartans come in a wide variety of colours and patterns.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATartans.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/1970s_Missoni_sweater_and_skirt_set%2C_purple%2C_red_and_green_plaid_knit.jpg/500px-1970s_Missoni_sweater_and_skirt_set%2C_purple%2C_red_and_green_plaid_knit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/1970s_Missoni_sweater_and_skirt_set%2C_purple%2C_red_and_green_plaid_knit.jpg/500px-1970s_Missoni_sweater_and_skirt_set%2C_purple%2C_red_and_green_plaid_knit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1970s Missoni tartan knit jumper (sweater) and skirt set","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1970s_Missoni_sweater_and_skirt_set%2C_purple%2C_red_and_green_plaid_knit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/K%C3%B6pergewebe_2x2.jpg/500px-K%C3%B6pergewebe_2x2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/K%C3%B6pergewebe_2x2.jpg/500px-K%C3%B6pergewebe_2x2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Visualisation of 2/2 twill weave: the black weft threads go two over then two under the orange warp threads, staggered by one thread each pass (resulting in a diagonal pattern). In the actual cloth, the white gaps would be closed.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AK%C3%B6pergewebe_2x2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Tartan_cloth_closeup.jpg/500px-Tartan_cloth_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Tartan_cloth_closeup.jpg/1280px-Tartan_cloth_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Tartan_cloth_closeup.jpg/500px-Tartan_cloth_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Close-up view of traditional tartan cloth, showing pattern of diagonal \"ribs\" of colour; this is a five-colour tartan, in scarlet red, black, yellow, azure blue, and crimson red.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATartan_cloth_closeup.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu